<title>SWEDEN: Iceland airport cargo volumes rise 25 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Iceland airport cargo volumes rise 25 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iceland's international airport at Keflavik handled 2,016 tonnes of freight in January, a 25 percent rise from the same month a year earlier, Iceland's civil aviation administration said on Monday.</p>
<p>The administration published the following figures about airport activity for the month.</p>
<p>						    Feb 1997	Feb 1996</p>
<p>KEFLAVIK INT'L AIRPORT</p>
<p> Cargo export (in tonnes)			1,415	   1,123</p>
<p>	 import					  601	     490</p>
<p> Total						 2,016	   1,613</p>
<p> Mail export (in tonnes)			    41		38</p>
<p>	import					   112	     118</p>
<p> Total						   153	     156</p>
<p> Passengers					 50,488	  42,208</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
